{% doc %}
Documents this app's resolved metafield namespace for the reel metaobject
reference. This used to be the ONE place the magic string appeared, with
callers capturing `{% render %}`'d output into a local variable — but
Shopify's theme editor preview wraps app-block-rendered snippet output in
"<!-- BEGIN app snippet: ... --> ... <!-- END app snippet -->" comments for
its own inspector, which corrupts a captured render into a string that
never resolves shop/product.metafields[...]. Callers now hardcode the
literal string directly instead of rendering this snippet — keep them in
sync with the value below if it ever changes.

Confirmed empirically against a live product on the real storefront during
planning: product.metafields['app--404281098241'].reels is the working
access pattern. $app, plain "app", and combined "$app:reels" bracket forms
were all tried and do NOT resolve — this is not a guess.

@example
{% assign reel_namespace = 'app--404281098241' %}
{{ product.metafields[reel_namespace].reels.value }}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  echo 'app--404281098241'
-%}
